{"game": "alien-swarm", "language": "english", "appid": 630, "month": "2025-06", "window": 1, "start_date": 1748736000, "end_date": 1751327999, "month_true_total": 20, "quota": 20, "returned": 20, "pulled_at": "2026-10-06 01:11:40 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "198473382", "author": {"steamid": "76561199213982278", "personaname": "Just A Mango", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199213982278/", "num_games_owned": 52, "num_reviews": 51, "playtime_forever": 145, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 98, "last_played": 1751232210, "avatar": "531580668709d36bb700885d4ece85ee0712a907"}, "language": "english", "review": "An absolute TON of fun with friends. Like many people i got this just to get the TF2 parasite hat, but i had a lot of fun playing it with my friends. It reminded me ton of Left 4 Dead, Half life 2 (specifically episode 2 with the poison antlions), and Madness: Project Nexus, and the missions actually take pretty long if you dont know what youre doing like me. There are 4 different classes, Tech (aka engie, which is sometimes mandatory to beat the mission), Medic (aka Dr. Ludwig), Special weapons (aka Heavy Weapons Guy), and Sargent, (aka Soldier). There are 2 people per each class, so there are 8 playable characters in total, each with their own unique stats. Theres bosses, crescendo events, and much more. Definitely worth playing 15 years later. Also, if you dont have friends to play with, or cant find a lobby, you can also practice offline with 3 other bots. (btw the game is only 2 gigs large and takes like 0 ram to run)", "timestamp_created": 1751214042, "timestamp_updated": 1751216447, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.555071532726287842", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reac